FOR MONGODB COLLECTION

After cloning/pulling the project from GitHub:
1. Open MongoDB Compass.
2. Connect to: mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017
3. Import the JSON file from "mongoDB.json"
4. Make sure the database/collection matches the names used in the project.
5. Make sure MongoDB is running before starting the backend.

===============================================================================

FOR MYSQL DATABASE

The MySQL database is included in the repository as: sql/database.sql

After cloning/pulling the project from GitHub:
1. Open XAMPP and start MySQL.
2. Open phpMyAdmin.
3. Go to Import.
4. Select sql/database.sql from the project.
5. Click Import.

This will create the food_delivery database, its tables, and the initial restaurant/menu data.
Make sure your local .env has the correct MySQL settings.